Tiny recovered candidate true; votes 1; inliers 3/3; scale 2.0; angle 0.0; translation (4.0, -3.0); build records 12; recognition records 31; default-threshold found false.
\image(figures/gh_votes.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The shown scene basis casts one actual vote. All six ordered scene bases are examined; only one selected candidate is recovered. The six distance checks stop at the first matching scene point for each model point.)
\alttext(Two bar charts show six model frame attempts and insertions, then six scene frames, lookups, vote updates, tally comparisons and verification distances. The tables print actual normalized bins and the first scene-basis vote.)

A table key is floor(u/q),floor(v/q), packed into two signed 32-bit cells; q is the
invariant-coordinate bin width. All bucket records count, including repeated bases
from different model points. A matching bucket casts one vote per stored record.
After each scene basis, the unordered tally entries are compared with the global
best using a strict greater-than test. Equal maxima retain the candidate reached
first by this execution; unordered-map iteration does not define a portable
lexicographic tie rule.

The selected model basis (mi,mj) and scene basis (sa,sb) recover the complex
multiplier a=(sb−sa)/(mj−mi), then translation t=sa−a mi. Scale is |a| and angle
is atan2(Im a,Re a). The implementation verifies only this selected candidate.

> Preserve the original six-point model amid four distractors

Apply scale 1.7, angle 0.9 radians and translation (12,−8) to the original six
points, then append the same four distractors. The table uses q=0.05 and the scene
distance tolerance is 0.0001. The recovered transform and all six inliers match
the original demonstration. Full-scene and local panels distinguish the distant
clutter from the recovered model’s alignment; the zoom changes only view limits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gh_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/geometric_hashing.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> model{{0,0},{2,0},{1,1.5},{2.2,1.1},{.5,-.7},{-.4,.9}};
 auto scene=dm::geometry::geometric_transform(model,1.7,.9,{12,-8});for(auto p:std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D>{{-30,-20},{-25,-34},{-38,-12},{-20,-28}})scene.push_back(p);
 const auto built=dm::geometry::build_geometric_hash_run(model,.05);const auto r=dm::geometry::recognize_run(built.table,model,scene,1e-4,2);const auto&m=r.match;
 std::print("Applied scale 1.7, angle 0.9, translation (12, -8).\nRecovered scale {:.4f}, angle {:.4f}, translation ({:.4f}, {:.4f}); votes {}; inliers {}/{}; model basis ({}, {}) to scene basis ({}, {}).\n",m.scale,m.angle,m.translation.x,m.translation.y,m.votes,m.inliers,model.size(),m.model_i,m.model_j,m.scene_a,m.scene_b);
 std::print("\nBuild frame attempts {}; inserted basis records {}; occupied bins {}; scene frame attempts {}; actual bucket-record votes {}; recovered candidates {}; verification distances {}.\n",built.work.frame_attempts,built.work.insertions,built.table.bins.size(),r.work.frame_attempts,r.work.vote_updates,r.work.recoveries,r.work.distance_checks);
 const auto mapped=dm::geometry::geometric_transform(model,m.scale,m.angle,m.translation);std::vector<double> sx,sy,mx,my;for(auto p:scene){sx.push_back(p.x);sy.push_back(p.y);}for(auto p:mapped){mx.push_back(p.x);my.push_back(p.y);}
 auto full=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();full.points(sx,sy,"Scene",{148,163,184},7).points(mx,my,"Recovered",{220,38,38},4).legend({"Scene","Recovered"},{{148,163,184},{220,38,38}}).title("Entire scene").xlab("Scene x").ylab("Scene y");
 auto zoom=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();zoom.points(sx,sy,"Scene",{148,163,184},9).points(mx,my,"Recovered",{220,38,38},4).legend({"Scene","Recovered"},{{148,163,184},{220,38,38}}).title("Model region").xlab("Scene x").ylab("Scene y").x_limits(9,15).y_limits(-9,-3);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(full).add(zoom).size(1100,540).title("Original model and transform recovered amid unchanged distractors").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gh_original.svg");
 if(!m.found||m.inliers!=6||m.votes!=4)throw std::runtime_error("original similarity recovery");
}
