> Bin boundaries, reflection and the absolute basis cutoff

Floor bins are discontinuous. At q=0.5, the representable value immediately below
u=0.5 belongs to cell 0, while u=0.5 belongs to cell 1. Arbitrarily small perturbations
can therefore remove a vote near a boundary. Negative cells also use floor:
u=−0.1 belongs to cell −1, not cell 0. Quantization width is dimensionless in the
basis frame; the final tolerance is in scene units. They control different effects.

The exact similarity proof assumes nonzero bases. This implementation additionally
skips actual squared basis lengths below 10^-18. That fixed absolute cutoff is
not invariant under arbitrarily small rescaling, and rounded quotients can cross
bin boundaries even when exact quotients agree. Reflection changes the sign of v;
it is outside the orientation-preserving model used here.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gh_boundaries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/geometric_hashing.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const double below=std::nextafter(.5,0.);const auto left=dm::geometry::geometric_hash_bin(below,0,.5),right=dm::geometry::geometric_hash_bin(.5,0,.5),negative=dm::geometry::geometric_hash_bin(-.1,0,.5);
 const auto f=dm::geometry::geometric_hash_frame({1,1},{0,0},{2,0}),reflected=dm::geometry::geometric_hash_frame({1,-1},{0,0},{2,0}),tiny=dm::geometry::geometric_hash_frame({1e-10,1e-10},{0,0},{2e-10,0});
 std::print("| boundary input u | q | signed cell u |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {:.17g} | 0.5 | {} |\n| {:.17g} | 0.5 | {} |\n| -0.1 | 0.5 | {} |\n",below,left.u,.5,right.u,negative.u);
 std::print("\nOriginal frame v {:.1f}; reflected v {:.1f}; tiny squared basis length {:.3e}; tiny frame valid {}.\n",f.v,reflected.v,tiny.length_squared,tiny.valid);
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.7;box.height=1.9;box.font_size=22;
 d.node("below",{0,0},"u immediately below 0.5\nq = 0.5",box).node("cell0",{7,0},std::format("Floor cell u = {}",left.u),box)
 .node("at",{0,-3},"u exactly 0.5\nq = 0.5",box).node("cell1",{7,-3},std::format("Floor cell u = {}",right.u),box)
 .edge("below","cell0","floor").edge("at","cell1","floor")
 .text({3.5,2.1},"Adjacent representable coordinates can occupy different bins",24)
 .text({3.5,-5},std::format("Reflection changes v: {:.1f} to {:.1f}; tiny basis accepted: {}",f.v,reflected.v,tiny.valid),23).save_svg("build/gh_boundaries.svg");
 if(left.u!=0||right.u!=1||negative.u!=-1||reflected.v!=-.5||tiny.valid)throw std::runtime_error("bin and frame limits");
}
