> Count actual work without treating a hash lookup as a whole recognition

For N model points and M scene points, excluding the two basis points gives

$$
F_N=N(N-1)(N-2),\qquad F_M=M(M-1)(M-2).
$$
\alttext(For at least three points, the number of attempted model or scene frames is the number of ordered distinct basis pairs times the remaining point count.)

Counts are zero for fewer than three points. Degenerate bases still incur attempts
but do not insert or look up bins. Without degenerate pairs, offline storage has
F_N records. Online work also includes V actual bucket-record hits, tally comparisons
and first-hit verification, whose worst-case distances are N M. Each recognition
validates all supplied table ids and input points before work. With T stored entries,
average hash work is O(T+N+M+M^3+V+N M); hash internals can cost more. The largest
per-basis tally can contain O(N²) model bases. Selected primitive counts below exclude
validation, allocations, hash internals and arithmetic FLOPs; they are not timings.

The implementation examines every ordered scene basis, even after a good candidate
exists. It does not implement the early-success behaviour discussed in the original
paper. Use a fixed triangle and successively append the listed distractors to make
the cubic number of frame attempts visible without implying universal clutter success.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gh_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/geometric_hashing.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> model{{0,0},{2,0},{0,1}},clutter{{9,5},{-7,3},{12,-9},{-5,-11},{15,8},{-13,14},{21,-4},{6,17},{-19,-8}};const auto base=dm::geometry::geometric_transform(model,2,0,{4,-3});const auto table=dm::geometry::build_geometric_hash(model,.25);
 std::vector<double>x,frames,updates,distances;std::print("| scene points | actual frame attempts | cubic formula | actual bin hits | actual vote updates | distance checks | candidate found | inliers |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t count=0;count<=clutter.size();++count){auto scene=base;scene.insert(scene.end(),clutter.begin(),clutter.begin()+count);const auto r=dm::geometry::recognize_run(table,model,scene,1e-8,1);const auto m=scene.size(),formula=m*(m-1)*(m-2);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",m,r.work.frame_attempts,formula,r.work.bin_hits,r.work.vote_updates,r.work.distance_checks,r.match.found,r.match.inliers);x.push_back(m);frames.push_back(r.work.frame_attempts);updates.push_back(r.work.vote_updates);distances.push_back(r.work.distance_checks);if(r.work.frame_attempts!=formula)throw std::runtime_error("actual cubic frame attempts");}
 auto f=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();f.lines(x,frames,"Frames",{37,99,235},2).points(x,frames,"",{37,99,235},5).title("All ordered scene frames").xlab("Scene points").ylab("Actual quotient attempts");
 auto v=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();v.lines(x,updates,"Votes",{220,38,38},2).points(x,updates,"",{220,38,38},5).lines(x,distances,"Distances",{22,163,74},2).legend({"Votes","Distances"},{{220,38,38},{22,163,74}}).title("Separate selected operations").xlab("Scene points").ylab("Actual primitive counts").y_limits(0,1.4 * *std::max_element(updates.begin(),updates.end()));
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(f).add(v).size(1100,530).title("Frame attempts, bucket votes and geometric checks are separate costs").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gh_work.svg");
}
