\caption(The fixed nine distractor coordinates are appended in the shown program’s order. Every frame-attempt count equals the cubic formula, including runs whose final candidate is poor. Vote and distance curves are observed for this one point set, not universal cost laws.)
\alttext(Tables and two line plots show actual work for scene sizes three through twelve. Frame attempts follow M times M-minus-one times M-minus-two; bucket-record votes and first-hit distance checks are shown separately with every found flag and inlier count retained.)

> Online complete records, ownership and strict inputs

Build traces emit each actual frame attempt and successful insertion. Recognition
traces emit scene frames, lookups, votes, tally comparisons, a completed recovery
and each checked distance. These are fixed-schema copied primitive records, with
no synthetic initial input record. A positive quota is checked before each append;
the default is one million records and zero disables only that optional quota.
Ordinary and run APIs have no trace quota. There is no numerical replay, partial
returned trace, truncation or caller mutation when admission fails.

This is an online event quota, not a precomputed whole-work estimate. The local
calculation can perform earlier work before rejecting the next record. Inputs,
root/work metadata, final ordinary table or candidate, working tally and allocator
storage are excluded. Complete records are not numeric entries or bytes, and the
quota is not a peak RAM limit. Copies of both records and ordinary results own
their data independently. Empty calls have zero records.

All point vectors must be finite and fit int ids. Quantization is positive finite;
tolerance is nonnegative finite with a finite square; min_votes is positive. The
entire public table’s stored ids must be distinct valid model-basis ids before
recognition or history work. That check cannot establish provenance: callers must
still pass the same ordered model used to build the table. Nonfinite intermediates
and out-of-range signed bin floors raise errors before casts. The fixed basis cutoff
returns an invalid frame rather than dividing by a degenerate basis.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gh_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/geometric_hashing.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> model{{0,0},{2,0},{0,1}};const auto built=dm::geometry::build_geometric_hash_trace(model,.25,12);const auto t=dm::geometry::recognize_trace(built.run.table,model,model,0,1,31);
 bool build_rejected=false,recognition_rejected=false,badpoint=false,badtable=false,badthreshold=false;
 try{(void)dm::geometry::build_geometric_hash_trace(model,.25,11);}catch(const std::length_error&){build_rejected=true;}
 try{(void)dm::geometry::recognize_trace(built.run.table,model,model,0,1,30);}catch(const std::length_error&){recognition_rejected=true;}
 auto invalid=model;invalid.back().x=std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN();try{(void)dm::geometry::build_geometric_hash_trace(invalid,.25,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){badpoint=true;}
 auto corrupt=built.run.table;corrupt.bins[0].push_back({0,99});try{(void)dm::geometry::recognize_trace(corrupt,model,model,0,1,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){badtable=true;}
 try{(void)dm::geometry::recognize_trace(built.run.table,model,model,0,0,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){badthreshold=true;}
 auto copy=t;copy.events[0].u=999;copy.run.match.translation.x=999;auto bcopy=built;bcopy.run.table.bins.clear();const bool owned=t.events[0].u!=999&&t.run.match.translation.x!=999&&built.run.table.bins.size()==6;
 std::print("| history | complete captured records | rejected cap | rejection observed |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Triangle build | {} | 11 | {} |\n| Triangle recognition | {} | 30 | {} |\n",built.events.size(),build_rejected,t.events.size(),recognition_rejected);
 std::print("\nIndependent copies {}; invalid final point before quota {}; invalid table id before quota {}; nonpositive threshold before quota {}; empty build events {}; empty recognition events {}; zero disables optional quota: {} records.\n",owned,badpoint,badtable,badthreshold,dm::geometry::build_geometric_hash_trace({}).events.size(),dm::geometry::recognize_trace({}, {}, {}).events.size(),dm::geometry::recognize_trace(built.run.table,model,model,0,1,0).events.size());
 auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(built.events.size()),11.},{"Captured","Rejected cap"});b.title("Online build events").xlab("").ylab("Complete records, not bytes").y_limits(0,15);
 auto r=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(t.events.size()),30.},{"Captured","Rejected cap"});r.title("Online recognition events").xlab("").ylab("Complete records, not bytes").y_limits(0,35);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(b).add(r).size(1100,500).title("Complete online traces reject one-record-short limits").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gh_controls.svg");
 if(!build_rejected||!recognition_rejected||!owned||!badpoint||!badtable||!badthreshold)throw std::runtime_error("online trace contracts");
}
