| Triangle recognition | 31 | 30 | true |

Independent copies true; invalid final point before quota true; invalid table id before quota true; nonpositive threshold before quota true; empty build events 0; empty recognition events 0; zero disables optional quota: 31 records.
\image(figures/gh_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The tiny build’s 12 records are six frame attempts plus six insertions. Its 31 recognition records are six frames, six lookups, six votes, six tally comparisons, one recovery and six distances. One fewer record rejects the complete returned history.)
\alttext(Two bar plots compare captured records and one-record-short rejected caps: 12 versus 11 for the build and 31 versus 30 for recognition. Printed controls verify deep ownership, complete invalid-input checks before quota and zero-event empty cases.)

The exact frame proof explains the method; actual execution exposes its limits.
Votes depend on quantized coordinates and bucket multiplicity, while first-hit
inliers depend on scene-unit tolerance and need not be one-to-one. The retained
original model is recovered at its original settings, and the same scene at a
coarser bin width refutes unconditional recognition claims. Constant point sets,
exact-rational grid checks and explicit distractors suffice here; no unrelated
external dataset or timing benchmark is needed.
